artifact.self_contained_problem:
For a field $F$, let $\mathrm{Br.dim}(F)$ denote the Brauer dimension of $F$, defined as the smallest non-negative integer $n$ such that for every central simple $F$-algebra $A$ one has $\mathrm{ind}(A) \mid \mathrm{per}(A)^{n}$, where $\mathrm{per}(A)$ is the order of the class of $A$ in the Brauer group $\mathrm{Br}(F)$ and $\mathrm{ind}(A)$ is the degree of a minimal splitting field; set $\mathrm{Br.dim}(F)=\infty$ if no such $n$ exists. Let $F(t)$ denote the field of rational functions in one variable over $F$.

Define a notion of "dimension" $\dim$, assigning a value $\dim F \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$ to each field $F$ in some sufficiently large and useful class of fields $\mathcal{C}$ (closed under the operation $F \mapsto F(t)$), such that the following two properties hold for every $F \in \mathcal{C}$:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\mathrm{Br.dim}(F) \leq \dim F - 1$;
\item $\dim F(t) = \dim F + 1$.
\end{enumerate}

